                "content": "\"\"\"GENERATED by tools/src/projection/providers/python/execution-projection-provider.ts — do not hand-edit.\n\nExecution ports for the projected kernel. ContractAdmissionError,\nExecutionAuthority, ExecutionObserver, and ExecutionStepObservation are\nimported from scenario_kernel.execution, not redefined.\nContractAdmissionError needs this because isinstance/except match by\nidentity; the other three need it for a more subtle reason, found by\nactually running mypy, not reasoned out in advance: they flow through a\nProtocol boundary (ExecutionAuthorityResolver.resolve's return type,\nSemanticExecutor.execute's parameter type, ExecutionObserver.observe's\nparameter type), and while the *Protocol* types themselves are\nstructurally matched, a plain frozen dataclass returned/consumed through\nthem is matched NOMINALLY by mypy — a freshly-generated\nExecutionStepObservation with an identical shape does not unify with the\nhand-written one the existing fixture-driven test doubles are typed\nagainst, even though both satisfy the Protocols they're used through.\nExecuteOptions doesn't have this problem: it never crosses a Protocol\nboundary, so it's fine as this generator's own type.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import Protocol, runtime_checkable\n\nfrom ..contracts import ContractReference, Disposition, Scenario, ScenarioEvent\nfrom ..execution import (\n    ExecutionAuthority,\n    ExecutionObserver,\n    ExecutionStepObservation,\n    ContractAdmissionError,\n)\n\n__all__ = [\n    \"ContractAdmissionError\",\n    \"ExecuteOptions\",\n    \"ExecutionAuthority\",\n    \"ContractValidator\",\n    \"ExecutionAuthorityResolver\",\n    \"SemanticExecutor\",\n    \"DispositionResolver\",\n    \"ExecutionObserver\",\n    \"ExecutionStepObservation\",\n]\n\n\n@dataclass(frozen=True)\nclass ExecuteOptions:\n    execution_id: str\n    root_execution_id: str\n    input: object\n    parent_execution_id: str | None = None\n\n\n@runtime_checkable\nclass ContractValidator(Protocol):\n    async def admit(self, contract: ContractReference, value: object) -> object: ...\n\n\n@runtime_checkable\nclass ExecutionAuthorityResolver(Protocol):\n    async def resolve(self, scenario_event: ScenarioEvent) -> ExecutionAuthority: ...\n\n\n@runtime_checkable\nclass SemanticExecutor(Protocol):\n    async def execute(self, authority: ExecutionAuthority, admitted_input: object) -> object: ...\n\n\n@runtime_checkable\nclass DispositionResolver(Protocol):\n    def resolve(self, scenario: Scenario, admitted_outcome: object) -> Disposition: ...\n"
